   $q$Why does the author call this path a "cycle"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The steps happen only on sunny days when there are no clouds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The steps repeat, and the last step leads back to the first one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The water moves in one straight line and then stops for good.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-sequence"},{"text":"Water only changes once, from a cloud into rain on the ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The steps repeat, and the last step leads back to the first one.$q$, $q$The last paragraph says "the sun warms the water again, and the cycle keeps going," so the end connects back to the start. The choice about water changing only once leaves out evaporation and condensation.$q$, 'draft', '00ec2600-e2e5-5534-b30a-bd1c559aee75')
